.TH MINTCAM 1 "October 2026" "MintCam 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mintcam \- webcam application for photo capture and video recording
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mintcam
.SH DESCRIPTION
MintCam turns a webcam into a live preview, photo capture and video
recording tool. It also handles QR scanning, focus assist, face auto
framing, time\-lapse, motion detection, background blur and RTMP streaming.
.PP
On first start the application creates a per\-user Python environment under
~/.local/share/mintcam/.venv and installs the Python dependencies it needs,
which requires a network connection and takes a minute or two. Later starts
just reuse it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/mintcam/.venv
Per\-user virtualenv with the runtime dependencies.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/mintcam
Settings and presets saved by the application.
.TP
.I ~/Videos
Default location for recordings.
.SH OPTIONS
This program takes no options.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.I QT_QPA_PLATFORM
Set to
.I xcb
or
.I wayland
to pick the Qt platform explicitly.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Start the application from the terminal:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mintcam
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The application closed normally.
.TP
.B 1
The application failed to start, for example because no webcam was found.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/jeaders/MintCam/issues
.SH AUTHOR
Alex Mirici
.SH SEE ALSO
The Software Manager entry for MintCam shows the same application with its
description and screenshots.
